A||N||5||kornholio||which one's the tach wire?||||5
Z||000000||kornholio||11-13-1999||02:23 PM||||I'm going to install a remote starter (V6 automatic), so I need to locate the tach wire.  At the coil, which wire is the tach wire?  There are two plugs that plug into the coil:   1 closest to the firewall and 1 closest to the trunk.  Both of these plugs have a white wire on the left and a red wire on the right.  Thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000001||kornholio||11-14-1999||09:47 AM||||Nobody has a remote starter for their Fiero?||||reg||5
Z||000002||Tim||11-14-1999||09:56 AM||||Try the white wire at the coil/tach filter or pick it up under dash pod.||||reg||1
Z||000003||kornholio||11-14-1999||11:56 AM||||Which white wire is the negative?  Are both of them negatives?  Does it matter which one I use?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tim||11-14-1999||12:36 PM||||Use the wire to the tach filter or from the tach filter to the dash pod.  I think this is the wire you are looking for.  I have the Whistler model WR9932.  I haven't installed it yet.  I plan on using the white wire at the dash pod.||||reg||1
Z||000005||batboy||11-14-1999||03:25 PM||||Tim's right about the tach gauge wire being white. The white tach wire come out of the distributor (along with a red wire) and plugs into the coil. The other coil plug is the same wires, the white wire goes to the tach filter, then continues on up to the instrument cluster.<P>Negative wires are generally black. If you need to find ground, they're everywhere. There should be a braided ground wire going to the truck lid hinge area. Use an eye connector and bolt any ground wires where the braided wire attaches to the body.<P>By the way Korny, thanks! When I went out to double check the wires on my 85 GT to make sure I had all this down correct, I discovered that the large coil wire that goes from the coil to the distributor cap was bad. It had a small hole in the insulation (it had been rubbing against the coil bracket) and looks like it's been arcing somewhat. Maybe that's the slight hesitation I've noticed every once and a while lately.<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 11-14-1999).]||||reg||1
